        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>Google Drive and Dropbox are fine for storing your everyday files, but if you\u2019re looking for a privacy-first alternative, check out <a href=\"https://filen.io/\">Filen</a>. It\u2019s an end-to-end encrypted cloud storage service that gives you 10GB of free storage and makes security the default instead of an extra feature.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The big selling point is something called zero-knowledge encryption. In basic terms, your files are encrypted on your device before they\u2019re uploaded, and only you hold the key to unlock them. Even Filen can\u2019t read what you store. Items such as tax documents, passport scans, family photos, or other sensitive files can be kept in the cloud for convenience, but they benefit from that extra layer of privacy.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Filen has apps for Windows, macOS, Linux, iPhone, and Android. You can also access it through your browser, with automatic ",
